The attached image (Figure 7D) is an immunoblot illustrating the production and secretion of IL-1β by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) under different stimuli. The cell lysate shows a 30kD pro-IL-1β band primarily when cells are primed with LPS, indicating its intracellular presence. Conversely, a 17kD active IL-1β band is prominently detected in the supernatant when cells are treated with Nano-11, with the strongest secretion occurring after LPS priming combined with Nano-11. This demonstrates that Nano-11 facilitates the cleavage and release of active IL-1β, a key pro-inflammatory cytokine.